{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1793662377245821001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"reservable-honeysweet-chrysalis","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"4fa5b38a3c6e65c4e9c7913bbad8a52f65673f9db984c5c6d79b4c35aff690de","event_uuid":"86daba33-34d9-4ea2-85ad-d02fe158445e","position":{"commit_sha":"e0f6ec807d698efced59d196b57d9a38e76ef186","position":"1793648054752089736-86daba33-34d9-4ea2-85ad-d02fe158445e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"54b528fea9c6a3665fc048f300b726e6d7a737f5db39e426cb06716c4de18a74","event_uuid":"6aba8c2c-d487-40fa-a3e2-92df13d72666","position":{"commit_sha":"dab2123841911e3eb41fd944610cc6d0c9f693cb","position":"1793648087406445447-6aba8c2c-d487-40fa-a3e2-92df13d72666"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1793648054752089736,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6aba8c2c-d487-40fa-a3e2-92df13d72666","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"fe94-2e22-ea9e-46f7"}],"description":"## Parent\n\nEpic `77e3-28e2-31ec-47ec`, authorized at full scope by the operator on 2026-11-02.\nThis is deliverable 6.\n\n## Depends on `fe94-2e22-ea9e-46f7`\n\nThe tidying janitor's review criterion is \"net LOC and non-positive mechanism delta\". The\nmechanism-delta half is exactly what the net-mechanism criterion story formalizes. Writing\nthis skill before that criterion exists would mean inventing a second, divergent\ndefinition of the same measure.\n\n## The gap\n\nThe janitor's PREMISE is sound: a deliberate pause between features to buy back\noptionality. Its objective function contradicts the premise in three architectural ways.\n\n1. **The Phase 2 floor selects for defects, not complexity.** Validity 0.75, impact 0.5,\n   reachable harm — these find bugs. Defect remediation adds mechanism more often than it\n   removes it. The 2026-08-29 run produced 37 items that were mostly ADDITIONS: oracles,\n   health commands, drift checks, metrics, pinning. The removals in that run came from the\n   operator manually expanding scope, not from the skill.\n\n2. **\"Never edits code\" turns tidying into ticket generation.** 20 to 37 tickets per run\n   enter the same pipeline that produces the complexity, with no net-LOC or net-mechanism\n   budget. Eight identical \"Restore headroom under the 800-LOC cap\" epics exist.\n\n3. **Plans are approved against a frozen snapshot while `main` moves.** The 2026-08-29\n   approvals ran to 09-02 and the dead-code validation recensused 98 commits later, so\n   cites were stale by claim time.\n\nThe evidence that this is self-defeating rather than merely inefficient: janitor\nremediation AUTHORED artifacts this program then deleted. RP-04's\n`REBAR_RECONCILER_WRITE_FACADE` switch, the 8 `*_seam_clean_heldout.py` tests and the\nconfig-ownership gate; RP-03's `_call_with_retry` and `CREATE_ROUTE` toggle; the 08-06\nrun's MCP drift gate and the complexity-baseline CI lock; the 08-29 run's alias tombstones\n(landed 09-04, deleted 3 days later) and its rejection of shared MCP contracts (followed\nby the parity manifest on 09-01, deleted 6 days later).\n\n## The change — modify, not discard\n\nKEEP: discovery, blind verification, prior-decision checking, one-at-a-time approval.\nThose four are what make the skill trustworthy and none of them is implicated.\n\nSPLIT into two skills:\n\n- a **tidying janitor** whose only admissible outputs are deletions and collapses, judged\n  at review by net LOC and non-positive mechanism delta, run between features\n- a **defect audit** — the current skill, substantially unchanged — run less often and\n  NOT called cleanup\n\nThen change the tidying janitor's contract:\n\n- a run is capped at a handful of tickets, each landable in one session\n- the run is measured by `main`'s LOC and mechanism count a week later, not by tickets filed\n- it files no gates; a finding that wants a gate becomes an idea for the operator\n- discovery is against a SHA, with approval and ticketization inside 24 hours or the plan\n  is discarded\n- no per-file mechanical sweeps; a condensation is one atomic change or is not done\n\nThe last one has its own evidence: the comment-condensation sweep the janitor seeded ran\nas roughly 1,700 per-file tasks whose commits invalidated cites in 6 breaking-pass stories\nand whose worktrees held the host's gate slots.\n\n## Explicitly NOT attributed to the janitor\n\nThe duplicate-ticket incident (tier-2 replay harness) and the mechanism ratchet (Track I\nepic) were not janitor output. Recording that here so the split is not justified by\nevidence that does not belong to it.\n\n## Provider neutrality\n\nrebar must support a wide variety of providers and models. Both skills are prompt-shaped\nartifacts and must not assume a single vendor's model, tool-calling syntax, or harness.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Two skills exist where one did: a tidying janitor and a defect audit. Verified by\n      the presence of both skill definitions.\n- [ ] The tidying janitor's admissible outputs are deletions and collapses only, stated\n      explicitly. Verified by reading the skill.\n- [ ] It declares a per-run ticket cap. Verified by reading the skill.\n- [ ] It declares a success metric measured on `main` a week later — net LOC and mechanism\n      count — and NOT tickets filed. Verified by reading the skill.\n- [ ] It states that it files no gates and that a gate-wanting finding becomes an idea.\n      Verified by reading the skill.\n- [ ] It states that discovery is against a SHA with a 24-hour approval-and-ticketization\n      window after which the plan is discarded. Verified by reading the skill.\n- [ ] It states that a condensation is one atomic change, prohibiting per-file mechanical\n      sweeps. Verified by reading the skill.\n- [ ] The defect audit retains discovery, blind verification, prior-decision checking, and\n      one-at-a-time approval. Verified by reading the skill, so the split is proven not to\n      have dropped the parts that worked.\n- [ ] The defect audit is not named or described as cleanup. Verified by reading the skill.\n- [ ] Neither skill names a specific model or vendor. Verified by a test or by reading.\n\n## Plan grounding\n\nExact file:line citations for `examples/agent-skills/rebar-janitor/SKILL.md`, its Phase 2\nfloor, its \"never edits code\" clause, and any test that asserts skill structure are being\nmeasured against `origin/main` and will be written into this description before plan\nreview is requested. This ticket is NOT ready for review until that is done.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","fe94-2e22-ea9e-46f7"],["parent","77e3-28e2-31ec-47ec"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"77e3-28e2-31ec-47ec","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["complexity-reduction"],"ticket_id":"6b48-37ea-a714-4545","ticket_type":"story","title":"Split the janitor: a deletion-only tidying skill with a net-complexity budget, separate from the defect audit","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["86daba33-34d9-4ea2-85ad-d02fe158445e","6aba8c2c-d487-40fa-a3e2-92df13d72666"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793662377245821001,"uuid":"a7c0eda2-4cca-48cb-88d4-503f5ef3e97b"}